# Cloud Build source upload filter for image-build/cloudbuild-hub-gke.yaml.
#
# Derived from gcloudignore-omni, which keeps the web source that the root
# Dockerfile's frontend stage builds (`npm ci && npm run build`). The
# exclusions are the same as omni's.
#
# Gitignore semantics: a pattern without a slash matches at any depth.
# Unanchored, `agents.md`, `.gemini/`, `.claude/` and `README.md` would also
# drop files under //go:embed roots, e.g.
#   pkg/config/embeds/templates/default/agents.md   (pkg/config/init.go)
#   resources/templates/default/home/.gemini/       (resources/embed.go)
#   harnesses/claude/home/.claude/settings.json     (harnesses/embed.go)
# The build would still succeed, with those files missing from the binary.
# So, as in gcloudignore-omni and the root .gcloudignore, every pattern that
# names a repo-root file or directory is anchored with a leading "/"
# (patterns with an inner slash, such as web/node_modules/, are already
# anchored), and the few patterns left unanchored on purpose say why. The
# root .dockerignore anchors its equivalents, so the Cloud Build upload
# carries the same embed-root files as a local `docker build --target hub-gke .`.
#
# cmd/gcloudignore_contract_test.go checks that no tracked file under a
# //go:embed root is matched by any Cloud Build ignore file, including this
# one; cmd/dockerfile_contract_test.go checks that cloudbuild-hub-gke.yaml
# and image-build/README.md point at this file.
#
# Usage: pass --ignore-file=image-build/gcloudignore-hub-gke to
# gcloud builds submit (see cloudbuild-hub-gke.yaml).

#!include:.gitignore
# (gcloud resolves this next to this file: image-build/.gitignore, not the
# root .gitignore.)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Directories not needed by omni builds
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/changelog/
/docs/
/docs-repo/
/docs-site/
/examples/
/extras/
/hack/
/internal/
/reviews/
/scratch/
/scripts/
/shared-dirs/
/skills/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web frontend — INCLUDE source for omni (unlike .gcloudignore).
# Only exclude build artifacts and tooling detritus.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
web/node_modules/
web/coverage/
web/.screenshots/
web/.env*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test files — Cloud Build compiles Go but never runs tests
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unanchored on purpose: Go tests sit next to the code in every package.
*_test.go

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build artifacts and tool state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .git/, testdata/ and downloads/ are unanchored on purpose:
#   .git/      - VCS metadata of any nested checkout is never build input.
#   testdata/  - Go test fixtures live next to each package (pkg/*/testdata)
#                and Cloud Build does not run tests.
#   downloads/ - agent/harness runtime downloads can land in any directory
#                (mirrors the any-depth downloads/ in .gitignore).
# Everything else here names a repo-root path and is anchored with "/".
.git/
/.claude/
/.design/
/.scratch/
/.tasks/
/.scion/
/build/
/.build/
testdata/
downloads/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CI / IDE / config files not needed for image builds
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.gemini/
/.geminiignore
/.github/
/.gitignore

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Root files not needed for image builds
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/claude.md
/gemini.md
/.claudeignore
/.dockerignore
/.coordinator-state.md
/.eng-manager-state.md
/agents.md
/CHANGELOG.md
/GLOSSARY.md
/LICENSE
/Makefile
/README.md
/pr-*-review*.md
